[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b[1m          \u001b[34m\"text\"\u001b[38;5;247m: \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m\u001b[48;5;234m\"Praxis AI Gateway —\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[44;65r\u001b[1;1H\u001b[3S\u001b[62;39H\u001b[32m Quarterly Performance Report\\nExecutive Summary\\nPraxis processed 4.7 million API requests in Q2 2025, with a 99.97% uptime\\nacross all production clusters. Average latency for proxied inference requests\\nwas 23ms (p50) and 89ms (p99), excluding model inference time.\\nKey Metrics\\n- Total requests processed: 4,712,583\\n- Unique models served: 47 across 12 provider backends\\n- Token throughput: 2.1 billion tokens (input + output combined)\\n- Cache hit rate for response rehydration: 73.2%\\n- MCP tool calls dispatched: 318,429 with a 99.4% success rate\\n- File search callouts executed: 89,217 across 156 vector stores\\n- Average fan-out per file search: 3.2 vector store queries\\nInfrastructure\\nThe production deployment runs 8 Praxis instances behind a network load\\nbalancer. Each instance handles up to 1,200 concurrent connections with\\nautomatic backpressure via Ping"]
[0.000, "o", "ora's H2 flow control. Filter pipelines\\nare hot-reloaded without droppin\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[K\u001b[1;66r\u001b[65;132H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m\u001b[48;5;234mg connections —\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[44;65r\u001b[1;1H\u001b[10S\u001b[55;147H\u001b[32m the Q2 rollout included\\n14 pipeline updates with zero downtime.\\nSQLite response stores are sharded by tenant, with automatic compaction\\nrunning every 6 hours. PostgreSQL is used for cross-region conversation\\nstate where durability requirements exceed what SQLite provides.\\nSecurity\\nAll inference traffic is authenticated via mTLS between Praxis and backend\\nproviders. The CPEX policy engine evaluated 1.3 million authorization\\ndecisions with Cedar policies, enforcing per-model and per-tenant access\\ncontrols. Content guardrails (NeMo) flagged 0.02% of requests for review.\\nRoadmap\\nQ3 priorities include streaming support for agentic loops, cross-request\\nconversation continuation, and expanded A2A protocol routing for\\nmulti-agent orchestration.\"\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[1m        }\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;247m\u001b[48;5;234m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[1m      ]\u001b(B\u001b"]
